module Core

### Marker protocol for types that may back an `Atomic[T]` cell.
###
### A type obeys `AtomicType` iff it lowers to a byte-or-larger machine integer
### that the hardware can load, store, and read-modify-write atomically without an
### emulation lock. That is exactly the fixed-width integers `S8`..`S64` and
### `U8`..`U64`. `S128`/`U128` are deliberately excluded — not every target has a
### lock-free 128-bit atomic — as is `Bool`, whose `i1` lowering is sub-byte.
###
### This is a pure marker (no required routines); it exists only to constrain
### `Atomic[T]` (`needs T obeys AtomicType`) so misuse is a compile error.
### :see: {Atomic}
protocol AtomicType
  pass